<<<
make. M. him repeat it, very rarely to repeat; He must be made to repeat it, very rarely made repeat.
===
**make.** *M. him repeat it*, very rarely *to repeat*; *He must be made to repeat it*, very rarely *made repeat*.
>>>

<<<
make-believe is the true form of the noun as well as the verb, & makebelief a false correction; to make believe has meant to pretend from the 14th c.
===
**make-believe** is the true form of the noun as well as the verb, & *make-belief* a false correction; to *make believe* has meant to pretend from the 14th c.
>>>

